-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",385,{
[12289]="7006B076\n1\tTravel with Rothog to the audience chamber\tSpeak to Rothog the Storm about the situation\n2\tTalk to Rothog\tRothog has requested your attendance in his questioning of Zarzíra Dawn-star.\n3\tTalk to Rothog in Dâr Laja\tFollowing Zarzíra's actions in his chambers, Rothog asks to speak to you.\n",
[12290]="70062F39\n1\tDefeat blight-callers (total: 8)\030Defeat war-mongers (total: 4)\030Defeat blight priests (total: 4)\tMedi has asked you to defeat gaunt-men at Dol Ernil. Dol Ernil is in northern Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Medi\tYou should let Medi know that there are far fewer gaunt-men to haunt her dreams. Medi is at Gerwyn's convoy.\n",
[12291]="700097DB\n1\tDefeat Gauradan Tribesman (total: 6)\030Defeat Gauradan Gorge-stalker (total: 4)\030Collect Makeshift Claws (total: 4)\tThe Gauredain prowl the hills and forests of Emyn Uial, north-west of Ost Forod. Robin Dunkley desires revenge for the death of Nat Rapkins and wants you to defeat the evil men that slew him. He has also asked you to bring him some of the Gauredain's unusual weapons.\n2\tBring makeshift claws to Robin Dunkley\tRobin Dunkley is in Ost Forod, in Tyrn Fornech of Evendim, south-east of Emyn Uial. You have defeated a number of the Gauredain that slew Nat Rapkins and collected some of their unusual weapons. Robin Dunkley will be pleased to hear the tale.\n",
[12292]="700617AC\n1\tExamine the slain goblin\tYou have discovered the remains of a slain goblin outside the long-abandoned Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.\n2\tEnter the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth\tThe Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth can be found in the northern reaches of the Yondershire. After discovering a slain goblin outside the Hunters' Hall, you suspect that someone is acting against the goblins at Bâr Faroth. You should investigate the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.\n3\tExplore the camp-site inside the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth\tThe Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth can be found in the northern reaches of the Yondershire. After entering the Hunter's Hall, you have discovered the light of a camp-fire. You should investigate the camp-site inside the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.\n4\tTalk to Anthandir in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth\tAnthandir can be found in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth. After entering the Hunter's Hall, you have discovered a Ranger of the North, Anthandir, and his faithful companion dwelling in the old ruins. You should talk to Anthandir and learn of his purpose at Bâr Faroth.\n5\tLay traps for the goblins at Bâr Faroth (total: 10)\030Retrieve Rangers' caches at Bâr Faroth (total: 6)\tIdeal trap locations can be found throughout Bâr Faroth. Anthandir has marked your map with the locations of several Rangers' caches at Bâr Faroth. Anthandir has requested your aid in laying traps for the encroaching goblins at Bâr Faroth. In addition, he has tasked you with retrieving several Rangers' caches from the ruins before they are discovered by the goblins.\n6\tDeliver the Rangers' caches to Anthandir in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth\tAnthandir can be found in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth. You have set traps for the goblins and retrieved several Ranger caches as Anthandir requested. You should deliver the caches to Anthandir at the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.\n",
[12293]="70052945\n1\tAccording to Odulf, the ghost of Old Mad Ubb is somewhere in Blómgard. You should search the barrels and crates to make Odulf feel better.\t\n2\tPick up the squirrel\tThe squirrel can be found in Blómgard. You should pick up the squirrel.\n3\tShow the squirrel to Odulf\tOdulf can be found in Blómgard. You should show the squirrel to Odulf.\n4\tScold Vulmar\tVulmar can be found in Blómgard. You should scold Vulmar.\n5\tRadagast can be found in Laerlad. You should bring the squirrel to Radagast.\t\n",
[12294]="7001557F\n1\tBring an infused sapphire to Fastarr\tFastarr has asked you to bring him an infused sapphire with which the qualities you desire may be bestowed upon your weapon.\n2\tTalk to Fastarr to travel to the Ghost-forge\tFastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. Fastarr has bidden you to speak with him when you are ready to seek out the forge, but warns you that some unnatural force appears to have taken control of it.\n3\tBring the empowered sapphire to Fastarr\tFastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. You should return to Fastarr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.\n",
[12295]="7006074F\n1\tLook for the ghostly figure\tThe ghostly figure can be found near the road south of Eitheldir in the western Angle. You should look for the ghostly figure.\n2\tExamine the disturbed ground\tThe dirt pile is near the road south of Eitheldir. You should investigate the pile of dirt.\n3\tSearch the rocky outcrop\tThe outcrop is in the south-western Angle. You have defeated a man who was masquerading as a ghost, and found a bag with a tin of white paint. Continue searching the rocky outcrop for clues as to why he was trying to scare people away from this area.\n4\tContinue searching for clues\tThe outcrop is in the south-western Angle. You have defeated a Man who was masquerading as a ghost. Search the area of the rocky outcrop he was lurking around for clues as to why he was trying to scare people away from this area.\n5\tFollow the path\tThe path is in the south-western Angle. The brigand was guarding a small path. You should investigate the path.\n6\tDefeat the relic hunter captain\030Defeat relic snatchers (total: 6)\030Defeat relic hunters (total: 4)\tRelic hunters and relic snatchers can be found in the south-western Angle. You should defeat relic hunters and snatchers.\n7\tReturn to the elderly couple\tWaltney and Garan Maythorn are in the south-western Angle. You should let Waltney and Garan know that the brigand pretending to be a ghost has been defeated.\n",
[12296]="70037E95\n1\tDefeat boars\tThe Eastfold is teeming with dangerous boars. By hunting them, you will be providing a service to its inhabitants.\n2\tDefeat boars (total: 6)\tThe Eastfold is teeming with dangerous boars. By defeating them, you will be providing a service to its inhabitants.\n3\tCompleted\tYou hunted many boars while following the trail of one monstrous boar, and the Eastfold is better for it.\n",
[12297]="70060010\n1\tTravel to Hlídborg\tHlídborg can be found in south east Câr Bronach. You should travel to Hlídborg.\n2\tFind evidence of Angmarim influence over the stone-giants\tHlídborg can be found in south east Câr Bronach. You should find some evidence of Angmarim influence over the stone-giants.\n3\tCollect Dourhand coffers (total: 8)\tDourhand coffers can be found at Hlídborg. You should collect any Dourhand coffers that you find.\n4\tBring the Dourhand coffers to Órug\tÓrug can be found at Leitstáth. You should bring the Dourhand coffers to Órug.\n5\tTalk to Kúzun at Leitstáth\tKúzun can be found at Leitstáth. You should talk to Kúzun.\n",
[12298]="7003EAFD\n1\tDefeat giants in the giants' valley (total: 6)\tThere are giants mustering in a valley east of the High Moor in the Trollshaws. While in the giants' valley, you should attempt to drive off the giants which have come down from the Misty Mountains.\n",
[12299]="70060572\n1\tMeet up with Ravaedron outside Fernbrake Cot\tRavaedron has asked to meet you at Fernbrake Cot, where he will give the painting to his friends.\n2\tTalk to Maddoc Stagshorn outside his home\tMaddoc Stagshorn stands outside his home, contemplating the gift.\n3\tTalk to Ravaedron at Fernbrake Cot\tRavaedron is at Fernbrake Cot, beaming with happiness.\n4\tDefeat beasts of the Angle near Fernbrake Cot and near Glynafon (total: 4)\030Meet up with the Ranger Idhrien outside Glynafon\tRavaedron encountered the Ranger Idhrien on his way to Fernbrake Cot, and he thinks you should aid her if you can.\n5\tGather wild herbs for Idhrien ([see journal]/5)\tThe Ranger Idhrien suggested that you could help her gather some of the wild herbs she needs for making poultices and other healing remedies for the Dúnedain.\n6\tGather wild herbs for Idhrien (4/5)\tThe Ranger Idhrien suggested that you could help her gather some of the wild herbs she needs for making poultices and other healing remedies for the Dúnedain.\n7\tBring the wild herbs you gathered to Ravaedron\tGathering the herbs has brought you quite near to Ravaedron. He will be pleased to bring the fruit of your labours to Idhrien.\n8\tDiscover what has upset Ravaedron\tRavaedron has seen something by the side of the cottage that has quite disturbed him.\n9\tTalk to Ravaedron by Fernbrake Cot\tRavaedron stands by the cottage of his friends, hurt by their dismissal of his gift.\n",
[12300]="7005296C\n1\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Legolas.\n2\tTalk to Legolas at the Beorninghús\tLegolas can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[12301]="70071B37\n1\tDefeat wights at Lâkindar (total: 8)\tYou should defeat wights at Lâkindar, allowing the bodies of these victims of Barkhûshim's cruelties to find peace. Lâkindar is in the far south-western corner of An Shêru.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many wights at Lâkindar, allowing the bodies of these victims of Barkhûshim's cruelties to find peace.\n",
[12302]="70019BD2\n1\tTalk to Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith\tMaliriel can be found in the field of Imlad Lalaith in the eastern reaches of Egladil, along the banks of the river Anduin. You have been asked to introduce yourself to Maliriel, the Mistress of the Feast for Lothlórien.\n",
[12303]="700377A3\n1\tDefend the Glittering Caves\tWithstand the enemy waves and protect the civilians at the centre of the Glittering Caves.\n",
[12304]="70037DDB\n1\tProtect the Caves\t\n",
[12305]="70041862\n1\tTalk to someone in Sarnhad about the troubles of Lebennin\tSarnhad can be found due east of Linhir in Lebennin. Erchar has asked you to travel into Lebennin and provide aid where you are able.\n2\tLight lanterns in Sarnhad (total: 6)\tLanterns can be found throughout Sarnhad in western Lebennin. Erianir has asked you to light the lanterns in Sarnhad.\n3\tChildren of Sarnhad can be found throughout Sarnhad in western Lebennin. Erianir has asked you to bring hope to the children of Sarnhad before they fall into despair.\t\n4\tTalk to Erianir in Sarnhad\tErianir can be found in Sarnhad in western Lebennin. You have lit many lanterns to aid in illuminating the Dawnless Day and comforted those too young to understand the trials of Gondor. You should speak to Erianir.\n",
[12306]="700544D8\n1\tDefeat the Gloom of Núrn in Mordor Besieged\tNone can say what ship bore him hither to Middle-earth before Númenor was lost, but once he accepted Sauron's gift he could no longer be counted among the Men of that land. He dwelt in Thaurband, a fortress in southern Mordor, not far from the inland Sea. It was from that keep that the fear of him spread, giving him a new title to replace the name he no longer needed. He became the Gloom of Núrn, though he did not stay there, and roved far and wide at Sauron's command.\n2\tDefeat the Gloom of Núrn in Mordor Besieged\tNone can say what ship bore him hither to Middle-earth before Númenor was lost, but once he accepted Sauron's gift he could no longer be counted among the Men of that land. He dwelt in Thaurband, a fortress in southern Mordor, not far from the inland Sea. It was from that keep that the fear of him spread, giving him a new title to replace the name he no longer needed. He became the Gloom of Núrn, though he did not stay there, and roved far and wide at Sauron's command.\n3\tThe Gloom of Núrn, defeated but enduring\tNone can say what ship bore him hither to Middle-earth before Númenor was lost, but once he accepted Sauron's gift he could no longer be counted among the Men of that land. He dwelt in Thaurband, a fortress in southern Mordor, not far from the inland Sea. It was from that keep that the fear of him spread, giving him a new title to replace the name he no longer needed. He became the Gloom of Núrn, though he did not stay there, and roved far and wide at Sauron's command.\n",
[12307]="7001CCD5\n1\tPlant the banner at the Gostannon\030Collect Banner of the Malledhrim\tThe pile of stones is atop a small rise in the Orc-camp at the Gostannon, north-east of Amon Angeled. Dannaswen has asked you to plant the banner of the Malledhrim at the Orc-camp near the Gostannon and defend it against the Orcs.\n2\tDefend the banner of the Malledhrim\tThe Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angened. Dannaswen asked you to defend the banner you planted in the enemy encampment at the Gostannon. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened\tDannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon. You should return to Dasswen with news of your victory.\n",
[12308]="70042F2B\n1\tInvestigate the ruins of Rolanthir\tRolanthir can be found just south of Faramir's Look-out in Southern Ithilien. You should investigate Rolanthir. Arodor has seen strange and ghastly lights coming from these ruins.\n2\tDefeat Darkwaters along the Morgulduin River (total: 6)\030Collect water samples from the Morgulduin (total: 4)\tRolanthir can be found just south of Faramir's Look-out in Southern Ithilien. You should defeat Darkwaters and collect samples of water from the Morgulduin River.\n3\tReturn the water sample to Arodor\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should speak with Arodor at Faramir's Look-out.\n",
[12309]="7001A631\n1\tSeek Nífdir in the Drownholt\tNenedhel parted ways with Nífdir to the west of Estolad Mernael. Nenedhel, leader of the Malledhrim in the Drownholt, has asked you to seek Nífdir in the swamp-lands.\n2\tTalk to Nenedhel at Estolad Mernael\tNenedhel is at Estolad Mernael, east of Nífdir's small camp. You should speak with Nenedhel and assure him that Nífdir is safe, but not yet ready to rejoin his companions.\n",
[12310]="70061FD7\n1\tDefeat goblins at Hove Farm (total: 12)\030Defeat Lukglob\tBethan Hove has asked you to defeat the goblins that have taken over her family's farm. The Hove family farm is in northern Cardolan.\n",
[12311]="70007A76\n1\tDefeat Nishrûk\tThe goblin's leader, Nishrûk, dwells in a goblin-fort built among the ruins south-east of The Forsaken Inn. Deputy Osmann has asked you to slay Nishrûk, the leader of the goblins troubling The Forsaken Inn.\n2\tTalk to Deputy Osmann\tDeputy Osmann awaits you across the bridge at the eastern edge of the ruins at Minas Eriol. You entered the ruins and defeated Nishrûk, as Deputy Osmann requested. You should return to him with news of your success.\n",
[12312]="700529DE\n1\tTalk to Skalla and ready the ambush\tThe stage is set for a battle between the goblin forces. You should complete 'Instance: Revenge of the Great Goblin.'\n2\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be found in Vegbár, the Beorning outpost in northern Wolf-denes. You should talk to Langhár.\n",
[12313]="7000A294\n1\tDefeat Wood-web spinners (total: 8)\030Defeat Wood-web hunters (total: 8)\tThere are spiders in the North Moors, south of Dwaling. Bob Greeneaves asked you to go out and slay spiders, in the hopes that the goblins will leave.\n2\tTalk to Bob Greeneaves in Dwaling\tBob Greeneaves is in Dwaling, north of the North Moors. You should return to Bob Greeneaves with news of your success.\n",
[12314]="70002CCD\n1\tCollect goblin-gems (total: 6)\tThe goblins of the Ram Dúath have stolen several treasures from the Suuri-lehmä. Aslak has told you that the gems might be found in chests within the Angmarim fort to the North-east.\n2\tBring the goblins' gems back to Aslak at Lehmä-koti\tYou have recovered several semi-precious gems stolen from the Surri-lehmä by the goblins of the Ram Duath. You must return them to Aslak at Lehmä-koti.\n",
[12315]="7006749D\n1\tSpeak with Gadnith in the easternmost outer courtyard\030Speak with the innkeeper at the central outer courtyard\030Speak with the dock-master on the shore west of the outpost\030Speak with the auctioneer\030Speak with Ledger-keeper Zarai at the courtyard in Jax Phanâl\tGirgish directed you to make your way around the outpost of Jax Phanâl to familiarize yourself with the citizens dwelling here. She then bids you return to her after meeting all the important folk in the outpost.\n2\tReturn to Girgish at Jax Phanâl\tHaving spoken with important members of the town, you should return to Khôltekh's emissary and let her know that you now have introduced yourself to those she recommended you meet.\n",
[12316]="700606AC\n1\tVisit the Erebor neighbourhood.\030Visit the central overlook\030Visit the Geode of Ironfoot Road\030Visit a modest home along the Wyrmhoard Bridge\030Visit a deluxe home along Oakenshield Way or Ironfoot Road\030Visit the kinship hall\030Visit Erebor Provisions and Crafting Hall\tThe entrance to the golden hoard can be found along the western walls of Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls in Erebor. You should visit and explore the newly-restored hall.\n2\tTalk to Gárthi Lockwarden\tYou should return to the entrance of the neighbourhood to speak with Gárthi Lockwarden.\n",
[12317]="70000022\n1\tBring the yeast to Gunderic Grubb\030Collect the yeast\tThe brigand camp is in the hills south of Woodhall, about midway between Tuckborough and Maggot's farm. The Golden Perch Inn is in Stock, east of Woodhall. Gunderic Grubb has sent you to search a brigand camp for his missing package of yeast.\n",
[12318]="7006C139\n1\tAcquire healthy boar slabs (total: 8)\030Cull aggressive sickly boars (total: 6)\030Cull feral sickly boars (total: 5)\tAcquire healthy boar slabs and cull diseased boars from the sounder.\n2\tFind the scout near the entrance to Shakhdag\tFind the scout near the entrance to Shakhdag.\n3\tDefeat Suginzi, the rot-boar\tDefeat Suginzi, the rot-boar.\n",
[12319]="7001949E\n1\tBring Celeborn's letter to Hrólfur\tHrólfur, an important overseer, can likely be found in the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Moria, in Durin's Way. Haldir has pressed you to bring an important message from Celeborn to Hrólfur after a previous attempt to make contact was spurned by the proud dwarf.\n2\tHelp the dwarves regain control of Lumul-nar\030Help the dwarves regain control of Nalâ-dûm\tHrólfur is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in Durin's Way. You should speak with Hrólfur and accept his two charges: the conquering of Nalâ-dûm, where the water-wheels are, and Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors.\n3\tTalk to Haldir at Talan Haldir\tHaldir awaits news of your good deeds towards the dwarves upon his flet near the River Nimrodel, on the western border of Lothlórien. You should seek Haldir and inform him of all that passed while you assisted the dwarves.\n",
[12320]="7001751A\n1\tDefeat Igash the Fanatic\tMany tribes of Orcs prowl the Grand Stair, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Geirr has asked you to defeat Igash in the Grand Stair without defeating any other members of the Moria Orc tribes. In doing so, you will assist in efforts to reclaim that cross-roads for the dwarves, and prove your great worth to Sigurd.\n2\tReturn to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall\tThe dwarf Sigurd can be found in the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Grand Stair. You have defeated Igash without defeating any other members of the Moria Orc tribes; Sigurd is waiting to hear of your foray.\n",
})
